---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About"
	description="AI product manager at Datadog. Personal blog on AI ethics, safety, and the impact of AI on society."
	pubDate={new Date()}
>
	<p>
		I'm Capucine, an AI product manager at Datadog, previously at Amazon.
	</p>

	<p>
		At Datadog, I work at the intersection of observability, alerting, and
		artificial intelligence, focused on one core problem: how to turn massive
		streams of signals into fast, reliable, and actionable decisions.
	</p>

	<p>My work centers on building critical feedback loops:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Detecting the right signals — not the noise</li>
		<li>Prioritizing based on real business impact</li>
		<li>Triggering intelligent responses, human or automated</li>
		<li>Continuously learning and improving the system</li>
	</ul>

	<p>I'm particularly interested in:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>AI-driven observability and predictive alerting</li>
		<li>Complex distributed systems — cloud, multi-service, AI infrastructure</li>
		<li>Turning data into strategic leverage</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Why this blog</h2>

	<p>
		Beyond my day job, I think a lot about the impact of AI on society — on
		minds, on ethics, on what we are willing to call safe, on whether we still
		know how to think critically when machines do part of the thinking for us.
		This blog is where I'll try to reason through those questions in public.
	</p>

	<p>
		Always happy to talk with people working on the future of AI and
		observability — find me on
		<a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/capucine-m-a3511385/">LinkedIn</a>.
	</p>

	<p>
		<em
			>Everything I write here reflects my own personal thinking, not the
			views of my employer.</em
		>
	</p>
</Layout>
